# --- Secrets: never commit -------------------------------------------------
# Applies anywhere in the tree, not just the one path that prompted it. A
# settings file that holds a credential is the single most common accidental
# commit, and the cost of the rule being slightly too wide is zero: the
# *.example templates below are what gets committed instead.
*.env
.env
.env.*

# Templates ARE committed. They carry placeholders, never real values.
!*.env.example
!.env.example

# Named explicitly too, so grepping .gitignore for it finds a hit.
guardrail-enforcement/demo/demo.env

# Local MCP server config — contains a live Phoenix bearer token.
.mcp.json
